course: dictionary
lesson: 13679
title: Words that are passed down
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: «Inherited» means passed down from someone who came before you. It comes from the verb «inherit», and its forms are inherit, inherits, inherited and inheriting.
explain: «Ben inherited curly hair from his mum.» Hair colour and hair type are passed from parents to children through the body, so inherited means it came to Ben from his mum in his body. The clue «from his mum» tells you who it came from.
explain: «Aunt Rose inherited a cottage from her grandmother.» Nothing passed through a body here. Aunt Rose received a home after her grandmother died. Read the whole sentence before you decide which meaning fits.
explain: Inherited can also mean got from someone who had something before you, like a job, a problem or old clothes. «Sam inherited his sister's old bike.» Ask yourself: who had it first? Then the meaning is clear.
fact: Inherited means passed down from one person to the next.
fact: Inherit is a verb, and inherited is its past form. It can also work as an adjective, as in «inherited traits».
fact: Eye colour, hair colour and blood group are inherited characteristics, passed on from parents through genes.
fact: Scars and speaking French are not inherited: they are learned or caused by what happens in life.
fact: In stories, a character might inherit a castle or a fortune after a relative dies.
exercise: «Mia has her dad's brown eyes, which she inherited from him.» What does inherited mean here? | *Passed down from her dad through his body | Lost in a game of hide and seek | Bought from a shop on the high street | Painted on a wall
exercise: «When her grandad died, Priya inherited his house and his garden.» What does inherited mean here? | Lost in a house move | Copied from a book | *Received from someone after they died | Painted in bright colours
exercise: «Tom inherited his big sister's worn-out school bag.» Which phrase means the same as inherited here? | Hid under his bed | Made himself from scratch | *Had passed on to him by his sister, who had it before | Stole from the lost property box
test: Which of these is an inherited characteristic? | *Freckles, passed down from parents through genes | Scars from falling off a bike | Speaking French | Mud on your shoes
test: «Grandma inherited a fortune from her uncle.» What did Grandma get from her uncle? | *A large amount of money, received after he died | A map of the stars | A tiny fish from the river | A new haircut
exam: Which sentence uses inherited to mean passed down through the body? | *«Leo inherited his grandad's grey eyes.» | «Leo inherited a job at the bakery from his friend.» | «Leo inherited a sailing boat when his uncle died.»
